<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan de Esquivel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1513</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan de Esquivel was a Spanish conquistador who crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> rising in Higüey, in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, in 1503–1504, capturing the cacique <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotubanama">Cotubanamá</a>. In 1509 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-columbus">Diego Colón</a> sent him to occupy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, where he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sevilla-la-nueva">Sevilla la Nueva</a> on the north coast and became the island's first Spanish governor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-de-esquivel.jpg" alt="Juan de Esquivel" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benedetto Bordone · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamaica_1528.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
